When an inline’s only in-flow child is a block, Ladybird preserves
line boxes for its nonzero inline-axis margins, borders, or padding.
It preserves the edges separately even when their widths cancel.

Gecko checks each margin, border, and padding edge separately in
nsInlineFrame::IsSelfEmpty(), including edges on split inlines.

Blink uses LineBreaker::HandleOpenTag() and HandleCloseTag() to
make nonempty inline edges create line boxes.

WebKit checks individual edges even when their total width is zero,
in LineRun::isContentfulOrHasDecoration(). Ladybird follows the same
rule, with its own inline-item and line-fragment representation.

Ladybird returns zero client dimensions for non-atomic inline boxes.
Blink’s Element::clientWidth() and Element::clientHeight() require a
GetLayoutBox() result, and WebKit’s counterparts require renderBox().
Gecko excludes non-replaced inline-flow frames in its implementation
of Element::GetClientAreaRect().
